        "After execution, the book_data/ folder contains 29 cleaned .txt files, one per novel.\n",
        "\n",
        "#2. Load and Transform Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "The cleaned texts must be converted into a Spark DataFrame suitable for annotation. Given the **4 GB RAM constraint**, each novel is split into **chunks of 3000 words**. This keeps individual rows small enough to be processed by the NLP pipeline without triggering out‑of‑memory errors.\n",
        "\n",
        "The loading step creates a DataFrame with two columns: `book` (the short title) and `text` (a chunk)."
      ],
      "id": "9c6023c7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: split-text-function\n",
        "#| code-fold: false\n",
        "\n",
        "def split_text(text, chunk_size=3000):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Split a long string into a list of chunks,\n",
        "    each containing approximately `chunk_size` words.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    words = text.split()\n",
        "    chunks = []\n",
        "    for i in range(0, len(words), chunk_size):\n",
        "        chunks.append(\" \".join(words[i:i+chunk_size]))\n",
        "    return chunks"
      ],
      "id": "split-text-function",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This simple whitespace‑based split preserves the raw surface form of the text, which is exactly what the NLP pipeline expects. The chunk size of 3000 was chosen empirically to keep individual rows small enough to avoid out‑of‑memory errors, while still providing enough context for the sentence detector and part‑of‑speech tagger to work accurately.\n",
        "\n",
        "No separate “load all books” DataFrame is created. Instead, loading, chunking, and annotation are performed book‑by‑book – an approach that fits both our memory constraints and the embarrassingly parallel nature of the task.\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Annotation Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "Annotation is performed with Spark NLP’s pretrained pipeline \"explain_document_ml\". This model provides:\n",
        "\n",
        "```         \n",
        "Sentence detection\n",
        "\n",
        "Tokenization\n",
        "\n",
        "Lemmatization\n",
        "\n",
        "Part‑of‑speech tagging\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "It is multilingual (hence the ml suffix) and works out of the box for French.\n",
        "\n",
        "We launch Spark through sparknlp.start() with a heap limit of 1 GB and set spark.sql.shuffle.partitions to 1 to minimize shuffle overhead on a single‑machine setup. For each novel we:\n",
        "\n",
        "```         \n",
        "Read the cleaned text from book_data/.\n",
        "\n",
        "Split it into 3000‑word chunks.\n",
        "\n",
        "Create a small DataFrame with one column text.\n",
        "\n",
        "Apply the pretrained pipeline.\n",
        "\n",
        "Write the resulting annotated DataFrame to Parquet (overwrite mode).\n",
        "\n",
        "Discard the data and move to the next book.\n",
        "```"
      ],
      "id": "c84ff935"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: annotation-pipeline\n",
        "#| code-fold: false\n",
        "\n",
        "import sparknlp\n",
        "from sparknlp.pretrained import PretrainedPipeline\n",
        "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
        "\n",
        "# Stop any previous Spark session to avoid port conflicts\n",
        "existing = SparkSession.getActiveSession()\n",
        "if existing:\n",
        "    existing.stop()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Start a Spark NLP session with limited memory\n",
        "spark = sparknlp.start(memory=\"1g\")\n",
        "spark.conf.set(\"spark.sql.shuffle.partitions\", \"1\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load the pretrained pipeline (will download once if not cached)\n",
        "explain_document_pipeline = PretrainedPipeline(\"explain_document_ml\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Process each book independently\n",
        "for book_title in all_urls:\n",
        "    file_path = os.path.join(\"book_data\", book_title + \".txt\")\n",
        "    if not os.path.exists(file_path):\n",
        "        print(f\"Missing {file_path}, skipping\")\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "\n",
        "    with open(file_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "        book_text = f.read()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Chunk the text\n",
        "    chunks = split_text(book_text, chunk_size=3000)\n",
        "    book_data = [[chunk] for chunk in chunks]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Create a DataFrame for this book only\n",
        "    df = spark.createDataFrame(book_data).toDF(\"text\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Run the NLP pipeline\n",
        "    result = explain_document_pipeline.transform(df)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Persist annotated data to Parquet\n",
        "    result.write.mode(\"overwrite\").parquet(f\"results/{book_title}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Done: {book_title}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"All 29 novels processed!\")"
      ],
      "id": "annotation-pipeline",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
